  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Loma Linda University 2026-2027 Catalog (effective Summer Quarter 2026) program page 'Nutrition and Dietetics - B.S. and M.S.' (coordinated program, School of Allied Health Professions). Students without a prior bachelor's degree complete this three-year program; both degrees are conferred simultaneously. The catalog publishes the curriculum split by Junior Year, Senior Year, and Graduate Year (not by quarter); year sums verified: Junior: 48, Senior: 38, Graduate: 48 = 134 = the catalog's 'Total Units: 134' for didactic coursework. The catalog separately states 'Affiliation and practicum units are required in addition to the didactic units listed above' and lists DTCS 778 (Clinical Nutrition Affiliation, 12 units); this seed encodes it as a fourth required term, so the seed total is 146 = 134 + 12, documented here rather than silently matching the 134. AHCJ 328 (Wholeness Portfolio I, 1 unit) carries footnote 1 'Register three times to fulfill unit requirement'; it is transcribed at the published 1 unit because the catalog's own Total Units 134 confirms the table values. DTCS 304 (Community Nutrition) fulfills the service learning requirement per footnote 2. Placeholder rows 'REL_ 4__ Upper-division religion' (3) and 'REL_ 5__ Graduate-level religion' (3) are encoded with explicit placeholder codes documented here. The Graduate Year 'Electives: Any graduate-level course approved by advisor' (9 units) is encoded as a choice slot with no fixed option list (advisor-approved). Normal time to complete: 3 years (2 years / 7 quarters undergraduate plus 1 year / 4 quarters graduate), full-time; part-time permitted. A 3.0 cumulative GPA at completion of undergraduate courses is required to progress to the graduate level. Prerequisites (82 transferable quarter units including the published GE domains; 3.0 GPA; interview) are documented here and not placed in any term. Per-course prerequisites are not published in the curriculum tables; the published year order is the official sequence, so prereq arrays are intentionally empty. program_type 'accelerated': the coordinated B.S.+M.S. compresses both degrees into a 3-year full-time curriculum (sequenced here as 4 terms), versus the standard separate-degree path; the catalog publishes only this combined sequence.",
